    <details class="faq-item" open>
      <summary>Is Lio really comparable to Füm?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Yes. Both Lio and Füm are nicotine-free, vapor-free flavored air devices that work through ritual replacement — giving your hands and mouth something to do while delivering natural aromatics. The core concept is the same. The key differences are in ingredients sourcing (Lio uses IFRA-certified EU organic ingredients), craftsmanship (Lio is handcrafted in the Netherlands), and price point (Lio's Journey Pack costs roughly half of Füm's).</div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How does Lio work without nicotine?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Research shows that 50–70% of habitual behavior is driven by the physical ritual — the hand-to-mouth motion, the deep breathing, the sensory trigger — not just the chemical substance. Lio targets this behavioral component by providing the same physical ritual with natural aromatics, helping your brain transition to a healthier pattern.</div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What are Lio's cores made of?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Each core uses medical-grade polyester fiber infused with 100% organic natural essential oils from IFRA-certified European farms. The formulations include natural plant extracts like peppermint, black pepper, cinnamon, and other botanical aromas — all blended in the Netherlands.</div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What if it doesn't work for me?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Lio offers a 30-day money-back guarantee. If Lio doesn't help, simply contact <a href="mailto:support@breathelio.com">support@breathelio.com</a> with your order number and you'll receive a full refund within 5–7 business days. No complicated forms, no hassle.</div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Why is Lio so much cheaper than Füm?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Lio is a direct-to-consumer brand produced in the Netherlands, which allows them to maintain premium quality while keeping prices accessible. They don't spend on major podcast sponsorship deals or retail distribution markups. Instead, they invest in ingredient quality and product craftsmanship — and pass the savings to you.</div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Is Lio safe to use?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a">Yes. Multiple third-party toxicology reports have been conducted on the inhalation of Lio's plant compounds. All ingredients come from IFRA-certified European farms and are produced by certified EU manufacturers. Lio is vegan, allergen-free, and contains no nicotine, chemicals, or vapor. Note: Lio is not a medical device or smoking cessation aid.</div>
